Anika Patel: quick note — I'm cleaning up the SDK snippets for streaming + retries + pagination across py/ts/go. Found three small but important issues in the current docs: missing stream close in the python example, inconsistent retry backoff wording in TS, and a pagination cursor edge-case for Go. I'll open a single PR that touches all three.
Tom Nguyen: thanks — can you drop the PR link when it's up? quick skim will help.
Anika Patel: PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4787 :changeset includes tiny edits and replacement samples. Highlights in the thread below.
Dev Docs Bot: Automated check: docs build + linkcheck started for PR #4787 :circleci: — will post results.
Samir Khatri: saw the python issue in a local repro — streaming generator didn't close on early return, leaking the underlying connection. Proposed patch looks fine, but can we also show the async context manager pattern as an alternate?
Anika Patel: good call. For python I added both patterns. Short snippets in the PR:

```python
# explicit close
resp = client.responses.stream("generate", input="...")
try:
    async for chunk in resp:
        process(chunk)
finally:
    await resp.aclose()

# context-manager (preferred)
async with client.responses.stream("generate", input="...") as resp:
    async for chunk in resp:
        process(chunk)
```

Tom Nguyen: nice. For TS I noticed our retry doc used fixed 2s backoff in prose, but code used exponential. We should make them match and add jitter sample.

Anika Patel: updated TS snippet to explicit exponential backoff with jitter and a comment about max attempts. New snippet:

```ts
// simple retry with expo backoff + jitter
const maxAttempts = 5;
for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= maxAttempts; attempt++) {
  try {
    const stream = await client.responses.stream({ model: 'x-small', input: '...' });
    for await (const chunk of stream) process(chunk);
    break; // success
  } catch (e) {
    if (attempt === maxAttempts) throw e;
    const backoff = Math.min(1000 * 2 ** attempt, 16000);
    const jitter = Math.random() * 300; // ms
    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, backoff + jitter));
  }
}
```

Luis Garcia: Go pagination note — when the cursor is the empty string we treat as end-of-stream in the example, but our SDK uses nil vs empty string depending on API version. PR should demonstrate checking both. Also add small example for reading pages until cursor=="".

Anika Patel: added this Go example to the PR to clarify behavior:

```go
// iterate pages until cursor empty
cursor := ""
for {
    resp, err := client.Embeddings.List(context.Background(), &api.ListEmbeddingsParams{Cursor: cursor, Limit: 100})
    if err != nil { return err }
    for _, item := range resp.Items { handle(item) }
    if resp.NextCursor == "" { break }
    cursor = resp.NextCursor
}
```

Samir Khatri: tiny nit — please add note in docs that some older pinned model versions may not support `stream()` and fall back to chunked polling. That helped one customer.

Anika Patel: added a short compatibility note + link to the model catalog. Also fixed two broken links the linkchecker flagged. Dev Docs Bot: build succeeded with one warning (line length) — posted details on PR.
Tom Nguyen: reviewed and left :+1: on the PR. LGTM from infra side (no runtime contract changes). Can you add me as reviewer for followups? I want to make sure we don't regress the retry wording elsewhere.
